    "1. Where the solid may become liquid during transport see 4.1.3.4.\r2. Liners of wooden IBCs shall be sift-proof.": 8,
    "1  IBCs shall only be used for free-flowing substances.\r2  Flexible IBCs shall only be used for solids.": 8,
    "1  Metal packagings, including inner packagings of combination packagings and outer packagings of combination or composite packagings, may only be used for packing methods OP7 and OP8.\r2  In combination packagings, glass receptacles may only be used as inner packagings with a maximum content of 0.5 kg for solids or 0.5 L for liquids.\r3  In combination packagings, cushioning materials shall not be readily combustible.\r4  The packaging of an organic peroxide or self-reactive substance required to bear an EXPLOSIVE subsidiary risk label (Model No.1, see 5.2.2.2.2) shall also comply with the provisions given in 4.1.5.10 and 4.1.5.11.": 8,
    "1  Cells and batteries shall be designed or packed to prevent short circuits and the dangerous evolution of heat.\r2  Protection against short circuits and the dangerous evolution of heat includes, but is not limited to:\r   - individual protection of the battery terminals,\r   - inner packaging to prevent contact between cells and batteries,\r   - batteries with recessed terminals designed to protect against short circuits, or\r   - the use of a non-conductive and non-combustible cushioning material to fill empty space between the cells or batteries in the packaging.\r3  Cells and batteries shall be secured within the outer packaging to prevent excessive movement during transport\r(e.g. by using a non-combustible and non-conductive cushioning material or through the use of a tightly closed plastics bag).": 8,
    "1  Packagings shall be designed and constructed to prevent the loss of water or alcohol content or the content of the phlegmatiser.\r2  Packagings shall be so constructed and closed as to avoid an explosive overpressure or pressure build-up of more than 300 kPa (3 bar).\r3  The type of packaging and maximum permitted quantity per packaging are limited by the provisions of 2.1.3.4.": 6,
    "1  Batteries shall be protected against short circuits.\r2  Batteries stacked shall be adequately secured in tiers separated by a layer or non-conductive material.\r3  Battery terminals shall not support the mass of other superimposed elements.\r4  Batteries shall be packaged or secured to prevent inadvertent movement.\r5  For UN 2794 and UN 2795, batteries shall be capable of passing a tilt test at an angle of 45° with no spillage of liquid.": 6
